---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Surface from '../components/Surface.astro';
import Pill from '../components/Pill.astro';
import PrimaryButton from '../components/PrimaryButton.astro';
import SecondaryButton from '../components/SecondaryButton.astro';
import Terminal from '../components/Terminal.astro';
import '../styles/download.css';

const latest = 'https://github.com/wheregmis/meroalpha/releases/latest/download';
const zip = 'MeroAlpha-Agent-macos-arm64.zip';
---
<Page title="Download MeroAlpha for macOS" description="Install MeroAlpha Agent on a Mac with Apple silicon, with one command or from the ZIP." current="/download">
  <main id="main">
    <Section id="download" class="download" title="Download MeroAlpha">
      <Fragment slot="intro">
        <Pill>macOS 14 or later · Apple silicon</Pill>
        <p class="lead">Two ways to install. Either way it’s a paper account in virtual NPR: no brokerage is connected and no real money moves.</p>
      </Fragment>

      <ol class="steps">
        <Surface as="li">
          <p class="kicker"><b>1</b> Recommended</p>
          <h3>Install with one command</h3>
          <p>It downloads the latest release and its checksum, checks the checksum, installs the app into Applications and opens it. Read <a class="link" href="/install.sh">the script</a> first if you like.</p>
          <Terminal lines={[{ label: 'In Terminal', command: 'curl -fsSL https://meroalpha.com/install.sh | sh' }]} />
        </Surface>

        <Surface as="li">
          <p class="kicker"><b>2</b> Or by hand</p>
          <h3>Download the ZIP</h3>
          <p>Unzip it and move MeroAlpha Agent to Applications. The app is ad-hoc signed, not notarized, so macOS blocks the first open: open System Settings › Privacy & Security and choose Open Anyway.</p>
          <div class="actions">
            <PrimaryButton href={`${latest}/${zip}`}>Download the ZIP</PrimaryButton>
            <SecondaryButton href={`${latest}/${zip}.sha256`}>SHA-256 checksum</SecondaryButton>
          </div>
          <Terminal lines={[{ label: 'Check the download, in the folder it’s in', command: `shasum -a 256 -c ${zip}.sha256` }]} />
        </Surface>

        <Surface as="li">
          <p class="kicker"><b>3</b> Then</p>
          <h3>Connect your agent</h3>
          <p>MeroAlpha works with an agent you install and sign in to yourself, over ACP. For Claude:</p>
          <Terminal lines={[{ label: 'Install the Claude agent', command: 'npm install -g @agentclientprotocol/claude-agent-acp' }]} />
        </Surface>
      </ol>

      <p class="note">Updates: the app checks GitHub’s public releases. See what changed in the <a class="link" href="/changelog">changelog</a>.</p>
    </Section>
  </main>
</Page>
